    skos:definition "Secondary 3D structure of a protein or peptide containing a right-handed coiled or spiral conformation, in which every backbone \\(\\ce{N-H}\\) group donates a hydrogen bond to the backbone \\(\\ce{C=O}\\) group of the amino acid four residues earlier."@en ;
